Z||000003||mrfixit58||02-24-2000||08:40 AM||||I never done the rear scoop but I have installed hood scoops, fender flares, and spoilers before (yes, I'm a chiled of the 60's).<P>Molding the rear scoop to the deck on a Fiero would be a piece-O-cake. Especially since the deck lid is not metal and the rear scoop comes with mounting bolt (I think thats right... Tom?).<P>Al you really ned to do is to grind off the paint and rough the deck surface and the mounting surface of the scoop. Buy some fiberglass filler called Mar-Glass (or equivilent). Use the Mar-Glass like glue to bond the scoop and secure the scoop with the retaining bolts. After it cures, sand off the excess. For the final finish, use Bondo, it easier to work. Remember, your only trying to conseal the seam so you don't need much. Prime and paint. The final finish wilbe dependent upon how well you prep.<P>Good luck,<BR>Roy L.||||reg||1
